  "notes": "Casual youth slang from English \"chill\" plus ⟦する→する：00392_suru⟧, meaning to relax and do nothing in particular. Closely related to the slang adjective チルい (chill, laid-back).\n\nREGISTER: Casual slang, mainly used by younger speakers since the 2010s–2020s. Avoid in formal writing or speech.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- ⟦{家|いえ}→家：00612_ie⟧⟦で→で：00502_de⟧チルする: to chill at home\n- ⟦まったり→まったり：09306_mattari⟧チルする: to chill out lazily",
